WEBVTT

00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:22.200
Agricultural Society

00:00:22.230 --> 00:00:25.290
Defense

00:00:25.310 --> 00:00:29.710
Agricultural Society

00:00:25.310 --> 00:00:29.710
Gate 
Closed

00:00:41.430 --> 00:00:44.690
Moyashimon

00:01:56.580 --> 00:01:58.230
What's that siren?

00:01:58.230 --> 00:01:59.130
Maybe there's a fire?

00:01:59.130 --> 00:02:01.830
<i>This is an announcement from 
the agricultural society.</i>

00:02:01.830 --> 00:02:05.960
<i>The 7th annual spring 
festival will now begin.</i>

00:02:05.960 --> 00:02:10.890
<i>I repeat: The 7th annual spring 
festival will now begin.</i>

00:02:06.460 --> 00:02:09.290
The Agricultural University 
Spring Festival Begins!

00:02:10.890 --> 00:02:11.880
Spring festival?

00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:13.480
What's that?

00:02:13.480 --> 00:02:14.390
No idea.

00:02:14.900 --> 00:02:18.830
<i>As of this moment, all the 
school gates are closed.</i>

00:02:18.830 --> 00:02:22.260
<i>Let's all have a good time 
putting our school's motto,</i>

00:02:19.400 --> 00:02:24.640
All 
Gates 
Closed 
for 
the 
Spring 
Festival

00:02:22.260 --> 00:02:24.660
<i>"Self-Sufficiency," into practice.</i>

00:02:25.310 --> 00:02:26.760
The spring festival...

00:02:26.760 --> 00:02:28.720
It's just starting out of the blue?

00:02:28.720 --> 00:02:30.670
She said the gates are closed.

00:02:30.670 --> 00:02:33.350
Was she serious? We can't go out?

00:02:33.350 --> 00:02:34.670
Probably just until evening, right?

00:02:34.670 --> 00:02:37.420
Agricultural 
Society

00:02:37.440 --> 00:02:39.910
1 Agri 
= 1 Yen

00:02:38.060 --> 00:02:41.950
Man, am I glad we ran into you guys!

00:02:41.950 --> 00:02:45.000
We have no clue what's going on.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:47.180
Where's Yuuki, anyway?

00:02:47.180 --> 00:02:50.980
Actually, I can't get a 
hold of him lately...

00:02:50.980 --> 00:02:52.310
So...

00:02:52.310 --> 00:02:55.940
School Ticket Exchange Center

00:02:52.310 --> 00:02:55.940
What are those "school 
tickets" supposed to be?

00:02:55.940 --> 00:02:58.920
For the duration of the spring festival, 
this campus is an independent nation.

00:02:58.920 --> 00:03:00.980
School tickets, or Agri, are currency 
exclusive to the festival.

00:03:00.980 --> 00:03:04.400
You can't buy from any of 
the stalls without them.

00:03:04.400 --> 00:03:05.710
What?

00:03:05.710 --> 00:03:08.720
They'll exchange our leftover tickets 
for cash when it's over, right?

00:03:08.720 --> 00:03:11.250
No, when the festival ends, 
the nation dies

00:03:11.250 --> 00:03:12.580
and school tickets become invalid.

00:03:13.060 --> 00:03:14.610
So don't buy more than you need.

00:03:14.610 --> 00:03:16.880
About 2,000 yen's worth should be plenty.

00:03:17.830 --> 00:03:19.690
Should be able to get five this year...

00:03:18.550 --> 00:03:21.010
So it's paper balloons and 
slapsticks this year?

00:03:21.410 --> 00:03:23.000
What are those for?

00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:26.010
The spring festival rules 
are different each year.

00:03:26.270 --> 00:03:29.420
Until certain conditions are met, 
the festival won't end.

00:03:30.260 --> 00:03:32.330
What's going to happen now?

00:03:32.330 --> 00:03:34.990
Sadly, they don't give any 
explanation of the rules.

00:03:34.990 --> 00:03:37.160
We have to discover them ourselves.

00:03:37.160 --> 00:03:38.500
Seriously?

00:03:38.500 --> 00:03:39.960
That's kinda scary.

00:03:39.960 --> 00:03:42.800
Well, if we just enjoy it normally,

00:03:42.800 --> 00:03:44.390
it should be over in three days or so.

00:03:44.390 --> 00:03:44.940
What?

00:03:44.940 --> 00:03:46.710
We can't leave the grounds 
for three whole days?

00:03:46.710 --> 00:03:47.460
Hurry up.

00:03:47.460 --> 00:03:49.040
Oh, okay...

00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:51.290
Agricultural Society

00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:51.290
Gate Closed

00:03:51.800 --> 00:03:54.040
Some weirdos are guarding the gate.

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:57.180
Athletic club members from 
the agricultural society.

00:03:57.180 --> 00:03:59.420
Would this all end if we defeated them?

00:03:59.800 --> 00:04:03.040
They look pretty tough, though...

00:04:04.810 --> 00:04:06.910
What are those posters?

00:04:06.910 --> 00:04:09.430
That's a bulletin board 
offering trades.

00:04:09.800 --> 00:04:13.220
For example, if our seminar 
brought in some fermented goods

00:04:13.220 --> 00:04:15.580
and traded them for 
meat and vegetables,

00:04:15.580 --> 00:04:16.940
we'd have a barbecue tonight.

00:04:17.480 --> 00:04:21.080
The Itsuki seminar's miso and soy 
sauce are popular every year.

00:04:21.080 --> 00:04:23.790
They're an indispensable part of 
Japanese eating habits, after all.

00:04:23.790 --> 00:04:25.130
Wow...

00:04:25.130 --> 00:04:28.540
We should have no trouble 
surviving on campus, then!

00:04:28.540 --> 00:04:31.580
Well, getting food is never 
a problem at this school.

00:04:32.080 --> 00:04:34.810
They should keep this bulletin 
board up all the time!

00:04:34.810 --> 00:04:36.270
They probably don't because there are

00:04:36.270 --> 00:04:37.560
people who'd never go home.

00:04:38.420 --> 00:04:40.460
Well, why don't we get 
something to eat?

00:04:40.460 --> 00:04:41.410
Sounds good.

00:04:42.590 --> 00:04:46.470
It's generally smarter to eat more 
expensive stuff on the first day.

00:04:46.770 --> 00:04:48.970
The festival could end tomorrow,

00:04:48.970 --> 00:04:51.990
and having school tickets 
after that will be useless.

00:04:53.010 --> 00:04:54.830
You're running a stall too, Professor?

00:04:54.830 --> 00:04:55.730
Indeed.

00:04:56.120 --> 00:04:59.000
Starting this year, professors 
are setting up stalls, as well.

00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:01.730
We'll sell rare items that will come 
in handy during the spring festival.

00:05:02.390 --> 00:05:04.490
So what are you selling, Professor?

00:05:06.740 --> 00:05:09.780
Oikawa-kun, Mutou-kun 
was looking for you.

00:05:09.780 --> 00:05:11.590
She wants you to help her 
eat the strawberries

00:05:11.590 --> 00:05:12.740
she got from another seminar.

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:13.970
Huh?

00:05:13.970 --> 00:05:16.020
She's in the lab. Go see her.

00:05:17.300 --> 00:05:19.170
Okay, then, I'm off.

00:05:20.690 --> 00:05:21.750
Now then...

00:05:22.140 --> 00:05:24.260
Whiskers, Fatso, and Shrimp...

00:05:25.640 --> 00:05:30.760
I bring good news to 
you unattractive men!

00:05:33.820 --> 00:05:36.900
The dream that men have 
attempted and failed

00:05:36.900 --> 00:05:38.770
to achieve for over 2,000 years...

00:05:38.770 --> 00:05:41.030
Once again, it is the 
power of microbes that

00:05:41.030 --> 00:05:43.320
will make their dream come true!

00:05:45.590 --> 00:05:48.200
Itsuki Keizou's special aphrodisiac set

00:05:48.200 --> 00:05:49.990
which will put any girl in 
the mood with one dose!

00:05:50.340 --> 00:05:51.200
Put girls...

00:05:51.200 --> 00:05:52.400
...in the mood?

00:05:52.400 --> 00:05:53.410
Aphrodisiacs?

00:05:53.600 --> 00:05:56.380
It even comes with a guide showing the

00:05:53.700 --> 00:05:58.040
Secret

00:05:56.380 --> 00:05:58.040
predicted outcomes for 
every girl on campus.

00:05:59.820 --> 00:06:01.670
So, buy these...

00:06:01.690 --> 00:06:03.530
Result of Experiment 
(With a woman, age 30, 
at a certain hotel)

00:06:02.570 --> 00:06:05.920
and get it on with your 
favorite girl now!

00:06:07.490 --> 00:06:09.230
First we have chocolate,

00:06:09.230 --> 00:06:11.540
the representative of aphrodisiacs 
throughout history.

00:06:11.540 --> 00:06:14.940
I've worked my own ideas into 
the fermentation of cacao,

00:06:14.940 --> 00:06:19.190
resulting in a bitter taste with 
even greater aphrodisiac power.

00:06:19.210 --> 00:06:29.530
Liqueur

00:06:19.750 --> 00:06:23.350
Herbs have also been long known 
to work as aphrodisiacs,

00:06:23.350 --> 00:06:26.730
but I've distilled my own 
unique assortment of herbs.

00:06:26.730 --> 00:06:29.700
There's no woman who wouldn't 
fall victim to this!

00:06:29.700 --> 00:06:32.040
Next we have Chinese 
herbal medicine with a

00:06:29.720 --> 00:06:41.120
Chinese Herbal Medicine

00:06:32.040 --> 00:06:33.810
history in aphrodisiac 
research that dates back

00:06:33.810 --> 00:06:35.090
to the late Han Dynasty.

00:06:35.090 --> 00:06:38.280
I've incorporated my own ideas 
in the fermentation stage

00:06:38.280 --> 00:06:41.960
to make women burn hotter and 
more intensely than ever.

00:06:41.960 --> 00:06:45.210
And here I have the representative 
of Japanese aphrodisiacs,

00:06:45.210 --> 00:06:47.220
a charred newt.

00:06:47.220 --> 00:06:50.450
Crush it into a fine dust 
and sprinkle it on your girl,

00:06:51.210 --> 00:06:54.220
and she'll instantly be 
at your beck and call!

00:06:56.100 --> 00:06:59.600
100,000 Agris

00:06:56.420 --> 00:06:58.250
100,000 agris?!

00:06:58.250 --> 00:06:59.580
So expensive...

00:07:01.890 --> 00:07:03.590
The sun's going down.

00:07:03.590 --> 00:07:06.910
I figured nobody would try 
to crash the gate today.

00:07:06.910 --> 00:07:09.120
The condition for ending 
this year's spring festival

00:07:09.120 --> 00:07:11.950
is to find the key and open the gate.

00:07:12.700 --> 00:07:15.070
Looks like nobody's figured it out yet.

00:07:15.510 --> 00:07:19.000
Offense

00:07:15.840 --> 00:07:16.730
Reserve corps!

00:07:16.730 --> 00:07:18.280
What are the students' plans?

00:07:18.280 --> 00:07:19.000
Sir!

00:07:19.590 --> 00:07:21.220
Eighteen clubs and labs are

00:07:21.220 --> 00:07:24.250
planning to drink outdoors this evening.

00:07:24.610 --> 00:07:25.650
All right!

00:07:25.650 --> 00:07:28.030
We make our move tonight at 1800 hours,

00:07:28.030 --> 00:07:30.150
and we start attacking at 2200 hours!

00:07:30.150 --> 00:07:33.260
This will be the true highlight 
of the spring festival!

00:07:40.750 --> 00:07:42.620
Aren't they going to eat?

00:07:43.540 --> 00:07:46.820
What should we do? 
Itsuki's shop is tempting.

00:07:46.820 --> 00:07:49.480
Guys were really flocking 
to that stall.

00:07:49.820 --> 00:07:53.060
But 100,000 agris means 
100,000 yen, right?

00:07:53.060 --> 00:07:55.490
That's insanely expensive!

00:07:55.490 --> 00:07:59.640
Still, leave it to Itsuki Keizou 
to make stuff like that.

00:07:59.640 --> 00:08:02.000
It just might be safe to 
trust in the results.

00:08:02.250 --> 00:08:03.840
But it's 100,000 agris!

00:08:03.840 --> 00:08:05.220
About that...

00:08:05.220 --> 00:08:07.230
There just might be a way to earn

00:08:07.230 --> 00:08:09.480
that much money at the spring festival.

00:08:09.480 --> 00:08:11.130
What are you three whispering about?

00:08:13.500 --> 00:08:15.330
We weren't whispering about anything.

00:08:16.750 --> 00:08:19.510
Then help us shut down the computers.

00:08:19.510 --> 00:08:20.420
Poncuters?

00:08:21.240 --> 00:08:22.800
Yes, to conserve energy.

00:08:22.800 --> 00:08:24.310
Starting this year,

00:08:24.310 --> 00:08:26.820
the school will generate 
its own electricity with

00:08:26.820 --> 00:08:29.650
the bio-gas plant for the 
duration of the festival.

00:08:29.650 --> 00:08:32.110
But its output is low,

00:08:30.480 --> 00:08:34.550
Recycle Center

00:08:32.110 --> 00:08:34.570
so consumption is going to 
be cut by 40% at night.

00:08:35.010 --> 00:08:37.040
What's a bio-gas plant?

00:08:37.040 --> 00:08:39.430
It turns animal feces and food scraps

00:08:39.430 --> 00:08:41.580
into energy through 
methane fermentation.

00:08:41.580 --> 00:08:43.830
This school is amazing sometimes.

00:08:45.820 --> 00:08:48.460
Okay, we're going to sleep 
in the fermenting cellar.

00:08:48.460 --> 00:08:49.910
See you tomorrow.

00:08:51.740 --> 00:08:54.920
Well, we have food in the lab...

00:08:54.920 --> 00:08:58.160
But how are we going 
to get 100,000 agris?

00:08:59.440 --> 00:09:01.620
Wait, have you guys

00:09:01.620 --> 00:09:04.560
decided who you'd use 
those aphrodisiacs on?

00:09:07.380 --> 00:09:09.820
I heard there's a temporary huge bath!

00:09:07.880 --> 00:09:11.070
Those three are the only women we know.

00:09:09.820 --> 00:09:11.280
You mean the forestry club's?

00:09:11.280 --> 00:09:12.880
Yeah! Want to go?

00:09:13.320 --> 00:09:14.320
Anyway...

00:09:14.320 --> 00:09:17.520
Let's head back to the 
dorm and start planning.

00:09:23.950 --> 00:09:25.710
Hey, Misato, Kawahama!

00:09:26.090 --> 00:09:28.330
We're all drinking! Join us!

00:09:28.330 --> 00:09:31.210
What a mess. 
It's a total sausage fest!

00:09:31.700 --> 00:09:32.890
What'd you expect?

00:09:32.890 --> 00:09:34.550
Everyone here is from our dorm.

00:09:34.550 --> 00:09:38.640
All the guys who are in seminars 
with girls are off with their seminars.

00:09:38.640 --> 00:09:41.890
Sorry, but we've got an 
important meeting to get to.

00:09:41.890 --> 00:09:43.250
We'll join you later.

00:09:43.250 --> 00:09:44.040
Okay!

00:09:51.650 --> 00:09:53.190
So basically,

00:09:53.630 --> 00:09:56.270
the question is who's going after whom.

00:09:56.270 --> 00:09:58.000
It sounds like we're discussing

00:09:58.000 --> 00:10:00.450
what we'd buy if we had 100 million yen.

00:10:00.450 --> 00:10:03.200
Sawaki, you'd pick Oikawa, right?

00:10:03.200 --> 00:10:05.800
Yeah. You seem to get along well.

00:10:05.800 --> 00:10:08.980
We just happen to be in the same class.

00:10:08.980 --> 00:10:12.460
We don't even have any 
female friends in our class.

00:10:13.340 --> 00:10:15.310
Kawahama, go for the grad student.

00:10:16.450 --> 00:10:19.220
Actually... I'd prefer Mutou-san.

00:10:19.220 --> 00:10:22.450
Hold on... I can't handle Hasegawa.

00:10:22.450 --> 00:10:24.350
She's out of my league, too.

00:10:24.560 --> 00:10:26.510
Didn't she change her lab coat

00:10:26.510 --> 00:10:28.850
to a double coat the day 
we joined the pre-seminar?

00:10:28.850 --> 00:10:30.300
How would I know?

00:10:30.300 --> 00:10:32.860
If you've been watching her 
that closely, you take her!

00:10:31.980 --> 00:10:32.750
Hey!

00:10:33.060 --> 00:10:34.220
Idiot!

00:10:34.220 --> 00:10:37.440
I'm telling you that I don't want 
an overbearing woman like her!

00:10:37.750 --> 00:10:43.080
I can't even imagine Hasegawa 
sleeping peacefully beside me.

00:10:43.080 --> 00:10:44.450
This conversation is pointless.

00:10:44.450 --> 00:10:48.650
A-Anyway, first we need to figure 
out how to earn the money.

00:10:48.500 --> 00:10:49.460
Yup.

00:10:49.460 --> 00:10:51.380
Well, it's 10 PM already.

00:10:51.380 --> 00:10:53.460
Let's just head back and 
drink with everyone.

00:10:53.930 --> 00:10:55.180
Yeah.

00:10:59.530 --> 00:11:01.540
Yer out!

00:11:01.940 --> 00:11:04.250
Wh-What the hell is all this?

00:11:04.640 --> 00:11:09.270
Offense

00:11:04.640 --> 00:11:11.640
Umpire

00:11:04.640 --> 00:11:11.640
Neutral

00:11:05.280 --> 00:11:06.980
Since your balloons are broken,

00:11:06.980 --> 00:11:08.850
we will confiscate your school tickets.

00:11:08.850 --> 00:11:10.000
You will be unable to buy

00:11:10.000 --> 00:11:11.650
anything until the spring festival ends.

00:11:11.990 --> 00:11:14.160
A surprise raid is really low!

00:11:14.160 --> 00:11:16.150
I bought 10,000 tickets!

00:11:16.620 --> 00:11:19.780
Fully understanding the rules is a 
necessity of the spring festival.

00:11:20.340 --> 00:11:22.370
When tomorrow comes, you should tell

00:11:22.370 --> 00:11:24.780
the surviving students 
what happened tonight.

00:11:26.180 --> 00:11:27.790
You suck, you monsters!

00:11:27.790 --> 00:11:29.060
Forget about making money...

00:11:29.060 --> 00:11:31.130
there's a rule that 
it can be taken away?

00:11:31.130 --> 00:11:33.750
Looks like it's best not to go outside.

00:11:33.750 --> 00:11:35.020
Let's just drink in our room.

00:11:37.070 --> 00:11:40.300
Spring 
Festival 
Day 
2

00:11:43.900 --> 00:11:46.610
What are you smoking out here for?

00:11:46.610 --> 00:11:47.430
Why shouldn't I?

00:11:48.130 --> 00:11:49.560
I won at rock, paper, scissors,

00:11:49.560 --> 00:11:51.280
so I took a break while you shopped.

00:11:52.030 --> 00:11:55.800
Last night's raid is the hot topic 
around the outdoor stalls, too.

00:11:55.800 --> 00:11:58.690
Taking their tickets 
was downright dirty.

00:11:58.690 --> 00:12:00.600
You think so, right?

00:12:00.600 --> 00:12:01.730
Look.

00:12:01.730 --> 00:12:04.320
The agricultural society was 
handing these out around the stalls.

00:12:04.870 --> 00:12:06.050
What's this?

00:12:06.050 --> 00:12:07.570
I think it's a chart of how

00:12:07.570 --> 00:12:09.990
many tickets the attackers 
took last night.

00:12:10.390 --> 00:12:13.700
In other words, 
if we defeat these guys,

00:12:13.700 --> 00:12:15.880
the amount of tickets written 
there will be ours!

00:12:15.880 --> 00:12:17.000
For real?

00:12:17.000 --> 00:12:20.760
I heard there were some guys who 
took revenge for last night,

00:12:20.760 --> 00:12:23.260
and they actually got 
tickets for winning.

00:12:32.230 --> 00:12:34.100
Another raid!

00:12:34.170 --> 00:12:36.690
Stay calm! There are three of us!

00:12:36.690 --> 00:12:38.940
We can win this! Get him, Sawaki!

00:12:38.940 --> 00:12:40.820
But I don't have a slapstick!

00:12:43.030 --> 00:12:44.360
More of them!

00:12:46.540 --> 00:12:47.410
What's going on?

00:12:47.410 --> 00:12:49.490
Hey! No running around in the lab!

00:12:49.490 --> 00:12:51.480
This isn't the time for that!

00:12:51.480 --> 00:12:53.650
Calm down... Just calm down.

00:12:53.650 --> 00:12:57.080
We're going to do awesome things 
with those 100,000 agris!

00:12:57.080 --> 00:12:58.880
They're sure enjoying this.

00:12:58.880 --> 00:13:00.710
Yer out!

00:13:00.710 --> 00:13:01.710
Huh?

00:13:01.710 --> 00:13:02.710
Us?

00:13:03.160 --> 00:13:05.790
Reserve corps are forbidden 
to enter buildings.

00:13:05.790 --> 00:13:08.600
Thus, the two on the 
upper floor are out!

00:13:08.600 --> 00:13:12.100
What the hell? Nobody told us that!

00:13:09.110 --> 00:13:10.480
What the...

00:13:10.480 --> 00:13:12.100
Looks like they're arguing...

00:13:12.390 --> 00:13:13.870
It can't be helped.

00:13:13.870 --> 00:13:17.980
We weren't informed of all 
the official rules, either.

00:13:18.880 --> 00:13:20.200
Aya-san?

00:13:20.200 --> 00:13:22.000
Would you open the door?

00:13:22.000 --> 00:13:23.230
I'll give you our tickets.

00:13:23.980 --> 00:13:26.240
Here you go. That's all of our tickets.

00:13:26.450 --> 00:13:29.450
I never thought I'd be 
called out up here...

00:13:29.450 --> 00:13:30.910
By the way...

00:13:30.910 --> 00:13:33.090
If you plan to attack them, 
this isn't the time.

00:13:33.090 --> 00:13:36.410
You'd best wait until the sun 
breaks through the clouds.

00:13:38.340 --> 00:13:41.320
I don't really get it, 
but I guess we're safe.

00:13:41.320 --> 00:13:43.510
We got 20,000 tickets.

00:13:43.780 --> 00:13:46.850
So the enemies don't 
know the rules, either.

00:13:46.850 --> 00:13:48.770
Which must mean that we have a better

00:13:48.770 --> 00:13:50.880
chance of success if we move fast.

00:13:50.880 --> 00:13:53.780
Aya-san said to wait 
until the sun comes out.

00:13:53.780 --> 00:13:55.260
Then what do we do?

00:14:00.020 --> 00:14:02.330
We won't get girls by 
just waiting around.

00:14:02.330 --> 00:14:04.860
We have to risk making a move.

00:14:05.460 --> 00:14:06.610
Okay, let's do it.

00:14:07.050 --> 00:14:07.740
Right.

00:14:07.740 --> 00:14:09.540
They're getting into this.

00:14:09.540 --> 00:14:11.240
Those three stooges...

00:14:11.660 --> 00:14:13.880
Breakfast served here!

00:14:13.880 --> 00:14:16.040
Come have your fill of animal proteins!

00:14:17.310 --> 00:14:19.540
I just noticed, nobody gets attacked 
around the outdoor stalls.

00:14:19.890 --> 00:14:22.790
If they did that, the stalls 
would be out of business.

00:14:24.760 --> 00:14:25.550
Hey, you guys!

00:14:26.720 --> 00:14:27.800
Want to buy some cigarettes?

00:14:28.780 --> 00:14:30.800
One pack for 1,000 agris, or 300 yen.

00:14:30.800 --> 00:14:32.170
1,000 agris?!

00:14:32.170 --> 00:14:33.410
That's robbery!

00:14:33.410 --> 00:14:35.680
Please! Think of it as fund raising!

00:14:35.680 --> 00:14:37.790
I exchanged 5,000 yen for tickets,

00:14:37.790 --> 00:14:40.190
and they were all taken 
in the raid last night.

00:14:40.680 --> 00:14:43.080
I've gotta get at least 
some of it back.

00:14:43.560 --> 00:14:46.940
Official

00:14:43.770 --> 00:14:45.170
Hey, you there!

00:14:45.170 --> 00:14:47.430
Are you selling goods 
without approval?!

00:14:47.430 --> 00:14:48.890
Crap, it's the special patrol!

00:14:48.890 --> 00:14:51.450
Don't tell anyone I was 
selling stuff for cash!

00:14:53.210 --> 00:14:54.490
What is that?

00:14:56.020 --> 00:14:58.960
The agricultural society's special 
patrol are the campus police.

00:14:59.780 --> 00:15:03.180
Once they capture someone 
conducting illegal activities,

00:15:03.180 --> 00:15:05.960
they're detained until 
the end of the festival.

00:15:07.230 --> 00:15:09.380
But you boys have nothing 
to worry about.

00:15:09.380 --> 00:15:11.470
You weren't involved.

00:15:12.070 --> 00:15:14.920
Well? Are you having any 
luck raising money?

00:15:14.920 --> 00:15:16.220
Uh, sort of...

00:15:17.010 --> 00:15:20.150
You'd better hurry. 
You're not the only ones looking to buy.

00:15:22.800 --> 00:15:23.750
Professor!

00:15:24.880 --> 00:15:26.730
Have you sold all the 
you-know-whats yet?

00:15:26.730 --> 00:15:28.100
No, not yet.

00:15:28.100 --> 00:15:30.360
Awesome! We're gonna buy them!

00:15:30.670 --> 00:15:33.250
Look, we're up to 50,000 agris!

00:15:33.250 --> 00:15:35.990
We're off to hunt more 
agricultural society guys now!

00:15:35.990 --> 00:15:37.850
We'll have a harem tonight!

00:15:39.340 --> 00:15:40.960
Off you go, then.

00:15:40.960 --> 00:15:41.980
Crap.

00:15:42.530 --> 00:15:44.000
We've gotta hurry.

00:15:56.720 --> 00:15:59.060
Don't falter! Take out the leader!

00:15:59.060 --> 00:16:00.600
They have strobe lights!

00:16:01.120 --> 00:16:02.600
They're just to distract you, Kawahama!

00:16:02.600 --> 00:16:05.670
Right! Use me as a stepping 
stone if you have to!

00:16:05.670 --> 00:16:06.110
Got it!

00:16:20.860 --> 00:16:21.860
What?!

00:16:33.540 --> 00:16:34.880
Prepare for the second offensive!

00:16:34.880 --> 00:16:36.110
Right!

00:16:49.660 --> 00:16:52.060
We can't beat the horse riding club.

00:16:52.060 --> 00:16:54.490
No way we can win.

00:16:54.490 --> 00:16:56.850
Forget sun, it's pouring.

00:16:56.850 --> 00:16:58.370
Let's just go home.

00:17:01.670 --> 00:17:04.380
We ended up staying 
hidden until nightfall.

00:17:04.380 --> 00:17:08.690
I'm beginning to think 100,000 
agris is beyond impossible for us.

00:17:08.690 --> 00:17:11.380
Right now, I just want a bath.

00:17:12.970 --> 00:17:15.460
Hey, Misato, Kawahama. 
We're just about to start drinking.

00:17:15.460 --> 00:17:17.390
You guys never give up...

00:17:17.830 --> 00:17:20.730
Don't be stupid. 
We've got nothing left to lose.

00:17:20.730 --> 00:17:22.340
We can afford to be bold.

00:17:22.340 --> 00:17:25.890
Wait, you guys are still 
alive? Incredible!

00:17:25.890 --> 00:17:27.130
Damn straight.

00:17:27.130 --> 00:17:29.790
We were just duking it out 
with the agricultural society.

00:17:29.790 --> 00:17:32.780
Though we spent most of the 
time hiding in the bushes.

00:17:32.780 --> 00:17:35.920
We're begging you. 
Get this festival over with, and fast!

00:17:35.920 --> 00:17:38.030
But we don't know how.

00:17:38.460 --> 00:17:41.570
About that... we've heard some 
things that could be useful.

00:17:42.600 --> 00:17:45.540
We've been out gathering information.

00:17:45.950 --> 00:17:49.830
First, there are limits on 
what those guys can do.

00:17:49.830 --> 00:17:52.920
They can't enter buildings.

00:17:52.920 --> 00:17:55.460
We already knew that.

00:17:55.460 --> 00:17:56.940
Oh, no, there's one more...

00:17:56.940 --> 00:17:58.680
a restriction that 
applies only to them.

00:17:59.190 --> 00:18:01.930
They can only attack in shadows.

00:18:00.740 --> 00:18:03.180
Yer out!

00:18:03.180 --> 00:18:04.380
Now I get it.

00:18:04.380 --> 00:18:06.740
So far, they've only 
been attacking freely

00:18:06.740 --> 00:18:09.220
at night or in the rain.

00:18:09.220 --> 00:18:12.400
That's why Aya-san said to 
wait for the sun to come out.

00:18:13.060 --> 00:18:15.470
Also, have you seen 
the guy who looks like

00:18:15.470 --> 00:18:17.670
their boss, sitting in front of the gate?

00:18:17.670 --> 00:18:18.930
Yeah.

00:18:18.930 --> 00:18:22.750
Our guess is that, if he's defeated, 
the spring festival will end.

00:18:22.750 --> 00:18:23.740
Seriously?

00:18:24.410 --> 00:18:27.220
But that area is in 
the shade all day long,

00:18:27.220 --> 00:18:29.670
and the defense looks tough. 
We can't take them.

00:18:29.670 --> 00:18:31.050
Indeed...

00:18:31.050 --> 00:18:32.250
But...

00:18:32.640 --> 00:18:35.380
Rumor has it that you get 
100,000 agris for defeating him.

00:18:35.890 --> 00:18:37.230
100,000 agris?!

00:18:37.230 --> 00:18:41.710
Well, to be honest, 
that rumor's not confirmed yet.

00:18:41.710 --> 00:18:43.670
What the hell? There's no point, then.

00:18:43.670 --> 00:18:45.910
You said it. Let's hit the baths.

00:18:45.910 --> 00:18:47.140
Hey, wait!

00:18:47.140 --> 00:18:49.180
We'll go dig up more info and report to you

00:18:49.180 --> 00:18:50.770
as soon as we can.

00:18:50.770 --> 00:18:53.560
But we want to ask one favor in return.

00:18:53.560 --> 00:18:54.270
Favor?

00:18:54.620 --> 00:18:56.600
You're in the Itsuki seminar, right?

00:18:56.600 --> 00:18:58.530
Please, set up a drinking party with

00:18:58.530 --> 00:19:00.150
the girls from that seminar for us!

00:19:02.140 --> 00:19:03.410
You get it, don't you?

00:19:03.730 --> 00:19:06.040
We want to drink with 
girls sometimes, too!

00:19:06.040 --> 00:19:08.020
Hasegawa-san is my favorite.

00:19:08.020 --> 00:19:10.000
I heard she comes from 
a really rich family.

00:19:10.000 --> 00:19:12.170
Think she dresses like 
that in the lab, too?

00:19:12.770 --> 00:19:15.230
Hasegawa-san is pretty popular.

00:19:15.230 --> 00:19:17.710
They just don't know 
what she's really like.

00:19:19.490 --> 00:19:25.300
Sorry, but tomorrow's out, 
and by the day after...

00:19:27.990 --> 00:19:30.180
We'll be devouring those girls.

00:19:30.330 --> 00:19:31.370
What?!

00:19:31.370 --> 00:19:32.190
Are you serious?!

00:19:32.730 --> 00:19:35.470
Well, when we're done,

00:19:35.470 --> 00:19:37.820
we'll tell Haruka or Aoi 
about your drinking party.

00:19:38.110 --> 00:19:39.350
Wow...

00:19:39.350 --> 00:19:40.350
He's a god!

00:19:40.350 --> 00:19:41.700
It's the advent!

00:19:42.000 --> 00:19:43.620
What the hell?

00:19:43.620 --> 00:19:47.250
He tasted a bit of reality in the 
first erotic story of his life.

00:19:47.250 --> 00:19:48.700
There's no stopping him.

00:19:52.150 --> 00:19:54.030
What's that evil chill in the air?

00:19:54.030 --> 00:19:56.540
It's because you show off 
your belly button every day.

00:19:56.540 --> 00:19:57.530
Oh, yeah!

00:19:57.530 --> 00:20:00.110
Why don't we go check out 
that huge bath today?

00:20:01.060 --> 00:20:03.220
Tomorrow is the big showdown...

00:21:24.920 --> 00:21:27.430
Moyashimon

00:21:24.920 --> 00:21:27.430
Episode 7

00:21:25.590 --> 00:21:27.430
Microbe Theater

00:21:25.770 --> 00:21:27.430
Microbe Theater 7!

00:21:27.970 --> 00:21:30.510
I haven't had a bath in two days.

00:21:30.720 --> 00:21:35.020
Resident Skin Microbes

00:21:32.170 --> 00:21:35.370
Hello! We're resident 
skin microbes!

00:21:35.370 --> 00:21:36.520
Good to see you!

00:21:36.520 --> 00:21:42.020
Resident Skin Microbes

00:21:36.770 --> 00:21:38.530
Boy, I tell you, we've really had our

00:21:38.530 --> 00:21:40.880
run of the place for 
these past two days!

00:21:40.880 --> 00:21:42.380
We're popping up everywhere!

00:21:42.380 --> 00:21:45.800
So we're going to tell all of you 
watching Microbe Theater today...

00:21:45.800 --> 00:21:48.030
...about the work that we 
skin microbes do for you!

00:21:49.870 --> 00:21:51.190
Hey!

00:21:53.290 --> 00:21:56.630
Hi! We're Staphylococcus!

00:21:56.630 --> 00:21:58.090
What a lively bunch.

00:21:58.090 --> 00:21:59.500
They're popping up everywhere!

00:21:59.500 --> 00:22:00.920
These guys...

00:22:00.920 --> 00:22:02.410
...live on humans...

00:22:02.410 --> 00:22:03.880
...and protect their skin!

00:22:05.380 --> 00:22:08.040
Our favorite food is human oil!

00:22:08.040 --> 00:22:08.970
They eat your oils...

00:22:08.970 --> 00:22:10.910
...and make your skin mildly acidic!

00:22:10.910 --> 00:22:12.150
Most microbes...

00:22:12.150 --> 00:22:13.940
...that are harmful to your skin...

00:22:13.940 --> 00:22:15.130
...don't like acid!

00:22:15.130 --> 00:22:16.350
I get it!

00:22:16.350 --> 00:22:17.890
By the way, who are you guys?

00:22:18.330 --> 00:22:20.960
I'm a Diptheroid, 
the cause of armpit odor!

00:22:20.960 --> 00:22:22.900
I'm M. furfur, and I'm known 
as a cause of dandruff!

00:22:24.920 --> 00:22:25.820
What is B. subtilis?

00:22:24.920 --> 00:22:29.910
In Microbe Theater Episode 8, We'll Do the Brewing.

00:22:25.820 --> 00:22:26.860
The Most Famous One is Natto

00:22:29.910 --> 00:22:32.470
Oh! What's wrong, Misato-kun?

00:22:29.930 --> 00:26:00.000
Next Week: 
"The Battle to Capture 
the Main Gate"

00:22:32.470 --> 00:22:34.410
Your face is all red!
